{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":39.88999938964844,"text":"The wall behind the altar is one single picture, floor to ceiling. Michelangelo painted it between 1536 and 1541, when he was over 60, a quarter of a century after he finished the ceiling. It shows the last day of the world, with hundreds of bodies rising and falling around Christ in the center. Many figures are twisted and muscular, like the Belvedere Torso, the statue Michelangelo loved in the courtyard. From 1980 to 1994, the whole chapel was cleaned, and under centuries of candle smoke, colors appeared so bright that some people refused to believe they were the originals.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.41999998688697815},{"word":"wall","start":0.41999998688697815,"end":0.6600000262260437},{"word":"behind","start":0.6600000262260437,"end":1.0199999809265137},{"word":"the","start":1.0199999809265137,"end":1.559999942779541},{"word":"altar","start":1.559999942779541,"end":1.559999942779541},{"word":"is","start":1.559999942779541,"end":1.8600000143051147},{"word":"one","start":1.8600000143051147,"end":2.2799999713897705},{"word":"single","start":2.2799999713897705,"end":2.759999990463257},{"word":"picture","start":2.759999990463257,"end":3.119999885559082},{"word":"floor","start":3.759999990463257,"end":3.759999990463257},{"word":"to","start":3.759999990463257,"end":4.440000057220459},{"word":"ceiling","start":4.440000057220459,"end":4.440000057220459},{"word":"Michelangelo","start":5.159999847412109,"end":5.659999847412109},{"word":"painted","start":5.659999847412109,"end":5.980000019073486},{"word":"it","start":5.980000019073486,"end":6.239999771118164},{"word":"between","start":6.239999771118164,"end":6.579999923706055},{"word":"1536","start":6.579999923706055,"end":7.71999979019165},{"word":"and","start":7.71999979019165,"end":8.15999984741211},{"word":"1541","start":8.15999984741211,"end":9.079999923706055},{"word":"when","start":9.479999542236328,"end":9.640000343322754},